                        "review": "MechanNIka huh... Agatha's Psychotic best friend who is tired of being unappreciated by her honestly very disfunctional and at times creepy family. The game is, like the later title, a simple adventure point-and-click game that wont take much time to finish at all, with an artstyle very remiscient of the early 2010s  and other media from that time such as Homestuck. Its clearly a project that has a lot of love behind it, even tho at times its own flaws may be visibile.\n\nThis game, as the first of what i like to call the Psychoverse of Mango.. is a little rough around the edges and while at times it might be as frustrating as Agatha Knife, with the same free exposure of sexual topics to a literal child which, aged horribly and i hope the devs have outgrown that by now... I would complain about the handwritten text like i did in my previous one but, i think that style actually fits better in this game due to its own age.\n\nThe one major advantage the first game has is that Nika, as the technological genius she is, is also an early alcoholic so she can drink her \"magic juice\" which can also give you hints about what to do next. Mind you, there's an achievement for not using this help, as well as one for not wasting money, which if you know how to pull it off, its really not hard at all to do. \n\nNot much else to say besides that i dont understand why people dislike Nika in particular so much, i found her much more tolerable and less creepy than Agatha, all things considered, even tho she indirectly got her own grandad killed... lmao\n\nScore: 7/10 (Nice game!)\nIf you like this game you may also enjoy Agatha Knife and, by extension: Colossus Down.",
